&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Help fans discover—and rediscover—the brands they love.&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring your curiosity, ideas and point of view to a team creating products, games and experiences enjoyed by fans around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About Hasbro&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hasbro creates joy and community through the magic of play. Across Hasbro, Wizards of the Coast and our partner network, teams bring iconic brands and new ideas to life through games, toys, entertainment and experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will support packaging development across Hasbro’s toy and game portfolio, with the chance to work on brands such as Nerf, Play-Doh, Star Wars, Transformers and Marvel. You will use ArtiosCAD to design and develop dielines and work with a cross-functional team to evaluate cost and help deliver projects on time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design packages that consider perceived value, aesthetic appeal and branding direction throughout the product development cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop packaging concepts through brainstorms and sketches for toys and games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create 2D and 3D CAD files for cost effective, sustainable and creative packaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create detailed packaging specifications and bills of materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype fully assembled packaging, including packaging whites and blisters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional partners to evaluate cost and keep projects on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you bring&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently enrolled in a university degree program in Packaging, Industrial Design, Graphic Design, Mechanical Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative and conceptual thinking, problem-solving and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to brainstorm package concepts and explain them through sketches and conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and manage multiple projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills and a team-oriented mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to improvement through personal goals and constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of 2D and 3D CAD in ArtiosCAD and SolidWorks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Adobe Photoshop is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work samples: &lt;/strong&gt;No portfolio is required. You may share sketches, CAD files, or a class, club, work or personal project that shows how you approach design problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Who can apply&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently enrolled in an accredited university degree program and will remain enrolled for at least one academic term after completing the co-op. Previous graduates are not eligible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can commit to the full program schedule and work model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You meet the work-authorization requirements stated below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed majors are examples. Related programs, coursework and transferable projects are welcome; previous internship or co-op experience is not required. If you do not match every preferred skill, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Opportunity details&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-op start and end dates: January - July 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule: Full-time, 40 hours per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work model: Hybrid&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Boston, MA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Application deadline: Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Pay and benefits&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a paid co-op. Hourly rates vary by degree level and year in school.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Boston hourly rate: $31 - $35&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What happens after you apply&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Early Careers team reviews applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Selected candidates will interview with the hiring team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Please keep your contact information and availability current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
