&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help fans discover—and rediscover—the brands they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring your curiosity, ideas and point of view to teams creating products, games and experiences enjoyed by fans around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;One application. Many ways to play.&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply once to this general application for consideration for anticipated Spring 2027 Project Management Co-ops based in Boston, Massachusetts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not one specific vacancy. Projects are confirmed on a rolling basis, and one application puts you in consideration across multiple opportunities with participating teams. You do not need to submit separate applications for each team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If your profile aligns with a specific co-op project, a recruiter may contact you directly with details and next steps. Applying does not guarantee an interview or placement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Hasbro&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hasbro creates joy and community through the magic of play. Across Hasbro, Wizards of the Coast and our partner network, teams bring iconic brands and new ideas to life through games, toys, entertainment and experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Teams and areas you may support&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on confirmed projects and business needs, your co-op could align to one or more areas such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project engineering &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(initial confirmed placement)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product development project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program and portfolio coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative or marketing operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital product and technology delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process improvement and change initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk, schedule and dependency management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our first confirmed placement is on a &lt;strong&gt;Project Engineering team&lt;/strong&gt;; other placements may open depending on business needs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Examples of what you may work on&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your placement, you may:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain project plans, milestones, trackers and clear status updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate meetings, decisions, deliverables and dependencies across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify risks or blockers early, gather context and help teams move toward solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn complex information into concise actions, timelines and stakeholder communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze a workflow or delivery challenge and recommend a practical improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support concept development, prototyping, product testing and manufacturing debug alongside engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create product specification packages that define content, functionality, and cost and delivery targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support retrospectives, documentation and repeatable ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are currently enrolled in a university degree program in Project Management, Business, Operations, Mechanical Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Design, Information Systems or a related degree program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to organize work, follow through and attend to both people and details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate information effectively with different audiences, including asking clarifying questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize, adapt and make progress when information is incomplete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with spreadsheets, presentation tools or project-management platforms is helpful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work samples: &lt;/strong&gt;No portfolio is required. You may share a class, club, work or community project that shows how you organized people and work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who can apply&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently enrolled in an accredited university degree program and will remain enrolled for at least one academic term after completing the co-op. Eligibility is based on program stage, not age.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can commit to the full program schedule and work model for the assigned location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You meet the work-authorization requirements stated below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Listed majors are examples. Related programs, coursework and transferable projects are welcome; previous internship or co-op experience is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
