&lt;h4&gt;Help fans discover—and rediscover—the brands they love.&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring your curiosity, ideas and point of view to teams creating products, games and experiences enjoyed by fans around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;One application. Many ways to play.&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply once to this general application for consideration for anticipated 2027 Summer Finance Internship opportunities in Boston, MA &amp;amp; Renton, WA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not one specific vacancy. Projects are confirmed on a rolling basis, and one application puts you in consideration across multiple opportunities with participating teams and brands. You do not need to submit separate applications for each team or brand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If your profile aligns with a specific internship project, a recruiter may contact you directly with details and next steps. Applying does not guarantee an interview or placement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Hasbro&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hasbro creates joy and community through the magic of play. Across Hasbro, Wizards of the Coast and our partner network, teams bring iconic brands and new ideas to life through games, toys, entertainment and experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Teams and areas you may support&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on confirmed projects and business needs, your internship could align to one or more areas such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial planning and analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accounting and controllership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treasury and capital markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial and brand finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance operations and transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Examples of what you may work on&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your placement, you may:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze financial and operating data and translate findings into useful insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support forecasts, budgets, reconciliations, controls, reporting or cash-management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reports, dashboards or presentations that make performance and trade-offs clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research business questions, market practices or regulatory topics and summarize recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve a finance process, control, model or recurring workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with finance teammates and cross-functional business partners on a meaningful project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you bring&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are currently enrolled in a university degree program in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business, Analytics, Mathematics or a related degree program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical thinking, attention to detail and a commitment to accurate work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain findings clearly to different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with spreadsheets and interest in learning financial systems or data tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about how finance shapes business choices and long-term value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work samples:&lt;/strong&gt; No portfolio is required. Relevant analysis, case competitions, student organizations or coursework may be highlighted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Find your party: your global intern community&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Level up together. All interns join one global cohort connected through shared, structured onboarding and weekly learning and development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own meaningful work tied to real business priorities, with mentorship and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build career skills through brand immersion and conversations with leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect with peers through networking and social experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer and give back alongside the intern community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Who can apply&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are currently enrolled in an accredited university degree program and will remain enrolled for at least one academic term after completing the internship. Undergraduate and graduate students are welcome to apply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We generally prioritize students entering the final year of their degree after the internship. Students at other eligible stages, including those with approximately two academic years remaining, are also encouraged to apply. Eligibility is based on program stage, not age.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can commit to the full program schedule and work model for the assigned location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You meet the work-authorization requirements stated below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed majors are examples. Related programs, coursework and transferable projects are welcome; previous internship experience is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this work excites you but you do not match every preferred skill, we still encourage you to apply. We value potential, curiosity, willingness to learn and different paths to the same capability.&lt;/p&gt;
