&lt;p&gt;Connect with peers through networking and social experiences&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Volunteer and give back alongside the intern community&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who can apply&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are currently enrolled in an accredited university degree program and will remain enrolled for at least one academic term after completing the internship. Undergraduate and graduate students are welcome to apply. MBA candidates: please see our separate MBA internship postings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We generally prioritize students entering the final year of their degree after the internship. Students at other eligible stages, including those with approximately two academic years remaining, are also encouraged to apply. Eligibility is based on program stage, not age.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can commit to the full program schedule and work model for the assigned location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You meet the work-authorization requirements stated below.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed majors are examples. Related programs, coursework and transferable projects are welcome; previous internship experience is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this work excites you but you do not match every preferred skill, we still encourage you to apply. We value potential, curiosity, willingness to learn and different paths to the same capability.&lt;/p&gt;
