&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Wizards of the Coast, we connect people around the world through play and imagination. From our genre-defining games like Magic: The Gathering® and Dungeons &amp;amp; Dragons® to our growing multiverse, we continue to innovate and build new ways to foster friendship and connection. That’s where you come in!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How would you like to use your leadership skills to nurture and grow a fun-loving and dedicated team of creative production artists that bringing some of Magic’s most exciting cards to life?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Magic: The Gathering is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Creative Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to define and grow our Production Artist team. This team builds custom frames and specialty print files that turn creative ideas into best-in-class collectible cards!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading a cohesive and high-functioning group of creative production artists by managing their workloads, developing their skills, keeping close tabs on resourcing, and encouraging a culture of inclusivity and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing a culture of teamwork and integration between the creative team, game production, and game design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with cross-functional teams within the studio to turn product goals into clear vision, deliverables, and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational instincts, including improving processes, creating documentation, coordinating reviews, and building repeatable workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;3+ years of creative leadership experience across diverse skills (art and design).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with licensed products, entertainment franchises, external creative collaborators, or brand extensions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fantastic communication skills and high comfort levels around giving and receiving feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail and highly developed organizational skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept in MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) and comfortable with remote collaboration tools (MS Teams, Smartsheet, Miro, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In compliance with local law, we are disclosing the compensation range for this role. The range listed is just one component of Wizards of the Coast’s total compensation package for employees. Employees may also be eligible for annual and long-term incentives. In addition, Wizards of the Coast provides a variety of benefits to employees. Here’s a look at what your benefits package may include: Medical, Dental &amp;amp; Vision Insurance, Paid Vacation Time &amp;amp; Holidays, Generous 401(k) match, Paid Parental Leave, Volunteer Program, Employee Giving &amp;amp; Matching Gifts Programs, Tuition Reimbursement, Product Discounts, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
