&lt;p&gt;Join Hasbro as a Systems Specialist for a maternity leave replacement (12 months) and become an integral part of our innovative team in Longueuil, QC, Canada. This outstanding opportunity will enable you to work on developing, improving, testing, and maintaining the system environments that support our creative and product development. You’ll work closely with experienced professionals to ensure our systems operate flawlessly and efficiently!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Perform as a Systems Specialist:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, improve, and test automated workflows supporting the development of products, digital, and printed assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support User-Acceptance-Testing of new or updated workflows by fixing errors and implementing testers’ change requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and build solutions to help systems’ day-to-day users manage their workload and measure their performance through data dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build searches to pull data from systems to support reports developed or used by day-to-day users and Data Analysts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop training materials and conduct training sessions for new system users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Digital Content Specialists to define and apply conventions and guidelines for maintaining an organized and secure systems environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new system features to improve day-to-day users’ efficiency and share with Process Managers and Digital Content Specialists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Will Bring:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills and ability to solve problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex processes and transform them into automated workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organizational skills with high attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage work under stress and meet tight deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous, self-motivated, and innovative demeanour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor’s degree in computer science or a related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability working with information or automated workflow platforms such as Esko WebCenter, Adobe Workfront, Monday.com, Power BI, Power Automate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability with product/creative development processes of consumer products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Java scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hasbro’s world-class brands and talented people are our greatest assets. One of the ways we invest in you is through a competitive and contemporary benefits package. Your particular benefits package will depend on your position, employment status, location, local legal requirements, and years with the company. Here’s a look at what your benefits package may include: Medical, Dental, Life Insurance, Health Care Spending Account, Disability Insurance, Wellness Subsidy, Paid Vacation Time and holidays, Generous RRSP match, Parental Leave Top-Up, Team Hasbro Volunteer Program, Employee Giving and Matching Gifts Programs, Toy Discounts and more!&lt;/p&gt;
