&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Are you ready to help lead the future of a galaxy far, far away?&lt;br&gt;Through our partnership with Disney and Lucasfilm, Star Wars represents legendary storytelling, cultural impact, and deep fan connection. We are looking for a commercially focused, curious, strategic, and driven Brand Manager to help guide the future of Star Wars at Hasbro.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be equal parts business manager, brand strategist, and product strategist. You will oversee global product development for the Star Wars Fan business while partnering with the global commercial teams to drive go-to-market planning, in-year line plan optimization, and profitable, sustainable, market share growth. Our ideal candidate possesses a strong work ethic and an appreciation for the joy that these toys bring to fans around the world. In this critical role, you will partner with cross-functional teams (design &amp;amp; development, packaging, engineering, demand planning, finance) on all phases of product development, business and line planning. As such, the successful candidate will need to be a strategic, high-energy, and collaborative thought leader with an ambitious spirit and curious mind. Creativity, ingenuity, and financial acuity will help you build foundational insights on how to grow the business. We are looking for someone to bring insights on what’s new and cool for our consumer with the ability to help translate those opportunities into new products and experiences for fans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Successful candidates have a deep appreciation for fandom, pop culture, and storytelling. They are proactive, energetic, collaborative, flexible, creative, analytical, strategic, and decisive - equally comfortable driving big-picture strategy and managing the details required to bring licensed products to market. They also prioritize relationships and the importance of teamwork.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective from the date that Hasbro opens its new Boston location, this position will be onsite Tuesday - Thursday at Hasbro’s new HQ in Boston, MA. In the interim, this position will be onsite Tuesday - Thursday at Hasbro’s HQ in Pawtucket, RI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Day in the Life as a Brand Manager:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive brand and product strategy for the Star Wars portfolio, supporting market share growth and long-term franchise health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage global product development and marketing processes, including line planning, portfolio optimization, and lifecycle management across multiple fan segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global commercial teams to support placement with key retailers and ensure the Star Wars product line delivers category leadership worldwide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Disney/Lucasfilm on content strategy, product approvals, and creative alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay on the pulse of fan behavior, media trends, and emerging play patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams - including regional marketing, consumer marketing, design &amp;amp; development, packaging, engineering, sales, demand planning, finance, and costing - to bring Star Wars products and experiences to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate consumer research, fan insights, market trends, and competitive analysis into clear, insight-driven strategies and stories for internal teams and retail partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Brand Marketing Managers and licensing partners on global briefs, brand positioning, and consumer-led marketing activation across digital, retail, and experiential channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own point-of-sale (POS) performance narratives, with a clear understanding of portfolio drivers, risks, and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support go-to-market planning, asset development, and messaging by providing product details, franchise context, and unique selling propositions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data and analytics to identify growth opportunities, inform pricing strategies, and balance revenue and margin goals in partnership with sales and finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience in consumer goods, brand/product management, business management, or marketing (licensed brands experience a plus).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong passion for storytelling, pop culture, and fandom - with the ability to balance creative integrity and commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally and influencing without authority in a matrixed, global organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical and creative strength: comfortable with data, financials, and spreadsheets, while also excelling at ideation and narrative-building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with international commercial teams and a strong understanding of omnichannel retail strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, with the ability to craft compelling business narratives for internal teams, licensors, and retail partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, collaborative mindset and an entrepreneurial spirit balanced with strong organizational navigation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with experimentation, risk-taking, and challenging the status quo while respecting brand and licensor guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to inclusivity, collaboration, and seeking diverse perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agility and resilience in a fast-paced, franchise-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The pay transparency range for this role is listed below. The hiring range will vary based on factors such as experience, skills, location and market conditions. Additionally, employees may be eligible for annual and long-term incentives as part of their overall compensation package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$124,800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$187,300 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Employees may be eligible for annual and long-term incentives as part of their overall compensation package, depending on role, location, and eligibility. Benefits and programs may include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Time Off to Recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
