&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Would you like to bring your passion for workplace safety, environmental compliance and continuous improvement to a company that is purposeful and a recognized leader in corporate social responsibility? The Specialist, Health &amp;amp; Safety supports Hasbro&#39;s Environmental, Health &amp;amp; Safety (EHS) programs across our offices and distribution centers. This role partners closely with the global Facilities, Sustainability, and local site leaders to keep our people safe and our sites compliant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Hasbro, we play and entertain with purpose! We are using our business as a force for good and building a safer, more sustainable company and world for all. We&#39;re passionate about play, protecting our people and our planet, and conserving natural resources for future generations. We are proud to have been recognized as one of 3BL&#39;s 100 Best Corporate Citizens!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Day in the Life of a Health &amp;amp; Safety Specialist.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance Reporting and Recordkeeping:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain OSHA 300/300A/301 injury and illness logs and post annual summaries for assigned sites. Track incidents, near misses, and workers&#39; compensation trends, and turn the data into monthly EHS metrics for site and global leadership. Manage the EHS reporting tracker and calendar so permits, inspections, and regulatory submissions are completed on time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-Site Safety Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a visible safety resource at offices, warehouses, and distribution centers. Conduct routine safety inspections, job hazard analyses, and ergonomic assessments, and follow corrective actions through to closure. Support incident investigations and root-cause analysis for injuries and near misses. Support programs such as Hazard Communication, fire safety, PPE, and emergency response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facility Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate fire and safety inspections, emergency evacuation drills, first aid/AED readiness, and site emergency response plans. Partner with Facilities and site leaders on safety for building projects, equipment installs, and contractor work. Maintain the chemical inventory and Safety Data Sheet (SDS) library for each site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environmental Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Support site hazardous waste and universal waste programs, including container labeling, accumulation-area inspections, manifests, and generator recordkeeping. Help maintain environmental permits and plans such as stormwater and air permits. Support annual environmental reporting, including chemical inventory (EPCRA Tier II), state hazardous materials submissions, etc.. Partner with the Global Sustainability Team on waste, recycling, and diversion data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training, Communication and Teamwork:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and deliver EHS training, including new-hire orientation, Hazard Communication, and emergency response. Support site safety committees by preparing agendas, minutes, and action-item tracking. Write safety talks, alerts, and lessons learned. Stay current on OSHA, EPA, and state requirements and help roll out corporate EHS initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in occupational health &amp;amp; safety, Environmental Health &amp;amp; Safety, Environmental Science/Engineering, Industrial Hygiene, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0 - 3 years of related experience in health &amp;amp; safety or EHS, ideally in an office, distribution center, manufacturing, or warehouse environment. Internships and co-ops count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of OSHA general industry standards and EPA hazardous waste (RCRA) requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in maintaining records and adhering to deadlines while paying close attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, comfort training and coaching employees at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using Microsoft tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to company sites and to walk warehouse floors and wear required PPE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot; data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The pay transparency range for this role is listed below. The hiring range will vary based on factors such as experience, skills, location and market conditions. Additionally, employees may be eligible for annual and long-term incentives as part of their overall compensation package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$76,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$114,800 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Employees may be eligible for annual and long-term incentives as part of their overall compensation package, depending on role, location, and eligibility. Benefits and programs may include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Time Off to Recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Financial Well-being&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Life &amp;amp; Family Support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Volunteer and Community Initiatives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Exclusive Perks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MailCompose&quot;&gt;Please review our &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;OWAf3b48604-66ff-cab5-fa36-85c2d05d437e&quot; class=&quot;OWAAutoLink&quot; href=&quot;https://nam11.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fdocs.hasbro.com%2Fprivacy%2Fjob-applicant&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CMaria.Hughes%40wizards.com%7C73f450b2476e4441be3308dec7006d14%7C701edd3ec7a84789b1ce8a243620d68f%7C0%7C0%7C639167001791388387%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=QzsYnPcynaB0OC2yYMSHab2TyW8jOlZQWyr87FBwDt8%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot; data-auth=&quot;NotApplicable&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; to learn how we collect, use, and protect your personal information in connection with the application process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
