&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Company&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Wizards of the Coast LLC&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Location&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 1107 Lake Washington Blvd. N #800, Renton, WA 98056&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Position Title&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Principal Business Intelligence Engineer (Recruitment #90944)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Job Description&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gather and analyze business requirements, design data models, and develop advanced Business Intelligence solutions. Collaborate with partners, conduct in-depth analysis, and understand business processes to provide actionable insights. Design and maintain Business Intelligence solutions and ensure data accuracy. Define data requirements and build automated data infrastructure. Develop data models and optimize pipelines. Elicit business needs and define key performance indicators. Provide recommendations and monitor key performance indicators. Work with multi-functional teams and communicate insights. Maintain proper documentation and offer training. Position is fixed location based in Renton office; however, telecommuting from a home office may also be allowed for up to 2 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Job Requirements&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requires a Bachelor&#39;s degree (or foreign equivalent) in Business, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a directly related field plus five (5) years of experience in business intelligence engineering and business analysis. Experience must include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Five (5) years of experience in each of the following (experience may be gained concurrently):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with BI tools such as Power BI or Tableau, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Advanced SQL skills for data extraction and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data modeling and ETL processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three (3) years of experience in each of the following (experience may be gained concurrently):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hours/week, 9:00am-5:00pm, Salary: $193,300-$196,300/year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
