&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Technical Sound Designer to join our digital game team at Wizards of the Coast. This role is anticipated to be a hybrid work position, with some work on-site and some work from home.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What You’ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop features, tools, and workflows that align with the game’s creative vision and enhance production efficiency, in collaboration with the Audio Director and key stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-discipline technical experts to streamline processes, improve integration, and elevate overall product quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with game engineers to implement scalable and reliable audio pipelines that support production at all stages.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize audio assets and development workflows to meet the evolving technical and creative needs of the project.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and troubleshoot issues across disciplines, providing clear technical solutions and support to team members.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author and maintain documentation outlining workflows, standards, and best practices for consistency and knowledge sharing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with QA teams to investigate, escalate, and track audio-related bugs, ensuring timely resolution of critical issues.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively monitor and address performance and memory challenges, maintaining audio quality and player immersion without compromising efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create audio content when required, applying strong sound design skills and proficiency with both commercial and proprietary tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with emerging audio technologies and innovations, translating them into technical direction and motivation for the audio team and project.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What You’ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of combined experience in the game industry as a Technical Sound Designer, deep familiar workflows as a Sound Designer, all contributing to high-quality game audio experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with AAA game engines, on the current pulse of emerging audio technology with a strong command of audio implementation and integration workflows/&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced expertise in MetaSound and Wwise, including setup, optimization, and troubleshooting within complex game environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Unreal Engine, Blueprint scripting, and engine tools that support&amp;nbsp; large scale audio implementation and authoring.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience designing and developing custom audio workflows and tools to enhance production efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative, with a demonstrated ability to partner effectively across departments and foster a strong team dynamic.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with scripting and level design tools, and well-versed in end-to-end game development pipelines across disciplines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-driven and proactive problem-solver, adaptable to feedback and capable of responding quickly to evolving project needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator, both written and verbal, with the ability to clearly convey technical and creative concepts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What Sets You Apart&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with coding or scripting (e.g., C++, Python, C#, or similar) is a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for video games and strong understanding of game audio industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in larger AAA games and the phases of development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
