&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Sourcing Manager, Technology Services to join our high-performing procurement team! In this position, you will champion sourcing, contracting, and supplier management for Technology &amp;amp; Digital Services throughout Hasbro, Inc. and its subsidiaries and affiliated entities, including Wizards of the Coast, LLC — handling an expansive, multi-entity portfolio covering SaaS, cloud, infrastructure, hardware, network, data centers, security tools, managed services, and IT professional services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Technology, Legal, Finance, and business partners across the enterprise to deliver outcomes that optimize speed, risk, and value. We adopt change, think big, and believe procurement is a strategic function — not just a back-office one.&amp;nbsp;In this role, you will handle the entire sourcing process for Technology &amp;amp; Digital Services — from RFQs and RFPs through supplier assessment, negotiation, and contract finalization — while owning the full contract lifecycle, including renewal planning, auto-renewal management, risk identification, and compliance monitoring. Partnering with IT Security, Data Privacy, and Enterprise Architecture ensures every vendor meets our compliance and risk standards before contract execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the commercial side, negotiating favorable terms — unit pricing, volume discounts, renewal price caps, payment terms, and SLA protections — goes hand in hand with capturing and reporting savings, cost avoidance, and working capital benefits through Hasbro&#39;s procurement savings framework. Spend data, market benchmarks, and vendor intelligence inform strategy and drive favorable pricing decisions across the portfolio. Your expertise in procurement will be crucial in driving outstanding results and flawless management of all sourcing activities. You will bring a proven track record of success and the ability to compete in a dynamic environment. You will Build structured Supplier Relationship Management programs that drive accountability, performance, and continuous improvement and champion sourcing processes and governance frameworks that scale across our enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Effective from the date that Hasbro opens its new Boston location, this position will be onsite Tuesday – Thursday at Hasbro’s new HQ location in Boston, MA. In the interim, this position will be onsite Tuesday –Thursday at Hasbro’s HQ in Pawtucket, RI or at Hasbro’s temporary location in Boston, MA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Day in the Life of a Sourcing Manager, Technology Services:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver measurable procurement value through structured sourcing execution, cost optimization, and supplier performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report efficiency using measurable savings and cost avoidance metrics to tell the complete value story&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance speed, quality, and risk to meet business objectives without compromising governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate &amp;amp; Influence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong connections with cross-functional collaborators across creative, technology, legal, and finance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence without authority by bringing insight, structure, and solutions to sophisticated business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead with Integrity&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with clarity and accountability in all sourcing and contracting activities, collaborating with suppliers in a mutually beneficial manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain Hasbro’s ethical standards, financial controls, and governance expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think Strategically&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employ market data and spend analysis to formulate and carry out sourcing strategies with collaborators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate risks and opportunities to support balanced business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adopt Innovation &amp;amp; Change&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the improvement of procurement approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring forward fresh insights, tools, and techniques to refine the sourcing and management of Technology &amp;amp; Digital services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop Self &amp;amp; Others&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate continuous learning and professional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share knowledge, mentor peers, and contribute to building procurement capability across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience in Business, Supply Chain, Finance, or a related field&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of procurement or category management experience concentrating on Technology &amp;amp; Digital Services categories — including software, SaaS, cloud, managed services, or IT professional services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated knowledge of Enterprise Architecture, Software Development Processes, and Information Security and Data Privacy considerations in vendor selection and contracting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading sourcing initiatives, supplier negotiations, and varied collaborator engagement across multiple business units or legal entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills with experience using spend data and market benchmarks to drive sourcing decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle competing priorities in a collaborative, fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, influencing, and relationship-building skills across technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with procurement platforms, contract lifecycle management systems, and spend analysis preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with vendor risk management processes and tools preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel approximately 10%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
