&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We&amp;nbsp;take play seriously. We’re looking for curious adventurers ready to find their party, fueled by imagination&amp;nbsp;and drive&amp;nbsp;to build what’s never been built before. At Hasbro and Wizards of the Coast, you’ll collaborate with passionate teams to reimagine our iconic brands and create experiences that spark joy, connection, and community through the magic of play. This is your chance to shape legendary play that lasts a lifetime.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Wizards of the Coast, we connect people around the world through play and imagination. From our genre defining games like Magic: The Gathering® and Dungeons &amp;amp; Dragons® and our Japanese TCG hit - Duel Masters, to our growing multiverse, we continue to innovate and build new ways to foster friendship and connection. That’s where you come in!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity for a &lt;strong&gt;Sr. Game Producer&lt;/strong&gt; to join the Duel Masters Studio! As a Senior Producer, you will lead all DM projects to completion, coordinating Game Design, Art, Editing, and Production to produce amazing looking products and experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do you have a passion for excellence with a proven track record of collaboration within a fast paced environment? We are looking for someone who can help us build and grow Wizard&#39;s future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guide and empower the team to define the vision, business, and production strategy for dozens of Trading Card Game releases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with internal and external teams to break out project deliverables and scope goals accordingly, and then build, prioritize, and maintain roadmaps, schedules, and documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify and address potential problems, resource blockers, quality concerns, and production velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build, improve, and iterate development workflow and processes to drive visibility and predictability for prioritized deliverables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent the needs of Wizards with all partners and vendors; driving all relationships involved with development with minimal direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Craft clear, detailed, and proactive communication to all Duel Masters team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliberately balance the goals of the players, the studio and the business using data to guide the conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate has a strong mix of creative, technical, innovation, and managerial experience from the live services and/or gaming space.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative oral and written communications skills in both English and Japanese.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of project management, process improvement,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to own a project from start to finish with minimal input from management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail balanced with strong drive towards delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, high-initiative person who encourages others and fosters an ownership-mindset in the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Trading Card games and/or the Japanese business environment is a bonus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
